// A numeric `as` to an INTEGER target honours its `?` / `!` suffix (D1041, DECISIONS.md
// §"Numeric `as` to an INTEGER target is exact-or-fail under the trio"). Before it was built
// the suffix was accepted and DROPPED — all three spellings compiled to the same
// `i32.trunc_f64_s` — so this probe is here to keep the capability, not to record a gap.
// The third cast is an out-of-range `i64`, which used to wrap to 2.
// Should print null then 3 then null
function ff64(x: f64): f64 { x }
function fi64(n: i64): i64 { n }
print(ff64(3.9) as? i32)
print(trunc(ff64(3.9)) as! i32)
print(fi64(4294967298) as? i32)
